and solutions that unifies social media publishing, engagement, and analytics across various channels; Sprinklr Insights, a suite of AI-based products and solutions that delivers consumer intelligence and helps to manage customer feedback; and Sprinklr Marketing, a suite of AI-based products and solutions that unifies content production and content lifecycle management with paid campaigns across various channels. The company also provides professional, implementation, managed, training, consultancy, and coaching services. The company has a strategic partnership with SocialEdge, Inc. to offers an integrated solution and an operating model for enterprise marketing, linking creator intelligence, social media management, and paid amplification within a unified ecosystem. Sprinklr, Inc. was founded in 2009 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Rory P. Read | President, CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $263K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 15%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $48K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $26K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Sprinklr, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.5B market cap on $857M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +6.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 72% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $158M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.95\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -11.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -30.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 148% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.4824636495796049},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (92% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.083},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 55/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Head to Head Contrast: Sprinklr (NYSE:CXM) versus Expensify (NASDAQ:EXFY)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/head-to-head-contrast-sprinklr-nysecxm-versus-expensify-nasdaqexfy.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793982530.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sprinklr (NYSE:CXM) Climbs Back: Is A Bigger Rebound Brewing?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/technology/sprinklr-nysecxm-climbs-back-is-a-bigger-rebound-brewing","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793617260.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sprinklr Bolsters Leadership Suite with the Addition of Three Senior Leaders to Help Accelerate Innovation, Drive Transformation, and Deliver Customer Value","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/articles/sprinklr-bolsters-leadership-suite-addition-130000760.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793883600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.937,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sprinklr's General Counsel Scott Jacob Sells 16,407 Shares at $6.97 Under 10b5-1 Plan","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/sprinklrs-general-counsel-scott-jacob-sells-1640